   "note": "the figure of chapter 30 for the distance of the sun (the circle of the sun about د with its diameter ج ا, the circle of the moon about ط and the circle of the earth about ن, their centres on the upright axis, which runs from the top of the sun's circle to the apex of the cone over س; the two sides of the cone from ج and ا, which touch the earth's circle at ك and م and meet at the apex; the two lines from ج and ا that touch the moon's circle at ه and ح and cross at ن, the one from ج running on to ض; the line from ه through ط and ح to ق on the right side of the cone; the diameter ك م of the earth; the line ع ف ض between the sides of the cone), measured with tools_s10/fig_measure.py at 600 dpi: the three circles and the nine lines are least-squares fits to their ink (stroke centres and widths), each line drawn between its meetings with the fitted circles and lines (the axis to the end of its ink; the line from ج to ض ends where it runs into the right side of the cone, 3.8 pt above the line ع ض, as in the print); the seventeen letters are set at the centres of their printed ink"
